  "clause_1_scope": "This Indian Standard (IS IS_12563) covers Indian Standard Specification / Test Method (IS IS_12563). This Indian Standard (First Revision) which is identical with ISO 2787 : 1984 'Rotary and percussive pneumatic tools — Performance tests' issued by the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) was adopted by the Sectional Committee and approval of the Basic and Production Engineering Division Council. The text of the ISO Standards has been approved as suitable for publication as Indian Standard without deviations. Certain terminology and conventions are, however, not identical to those used in Indian Standards. Attention is drawn especially to the following: a) Wherever the words 'International Standard' appear referring to this standard, they should be read as'lndian Standard'. b) Comma (,) has been used as a decimal markerwhile in Indian Standards, the current practice is to use a full point (.) as the decimal marker. This standard was first published in 1988 in two parts (Part 1 and Part 2), and both the parts were covering only data sheets for test reports. This revisio",
